# ==============================================================================
# Strange Lettractor environment (.env)
#   cp .env.sample .env
# The CLI loads .env from the working directory; every variable below is read
# by src/attractor/llm.lg, src/attractor/cli.lg or a dev/ live runner.
# Models are addressed as provider/name, e.g. anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-5.
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local let-go executable used by lgx and the dev runners (see README).
# LGX_LG=/path/to/let-go/build/lg
# Runtime used by the codex transport tests when it differs from LGX_LG.
# LG_EXECUTABLE=/path/to/let-go/build/lg

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenAI (native Responses API)  -> provider id: openai
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Anthropic (native Messages API) -> provider id: anthropic
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-api03-...
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com/v1
# Note: Claude Pro/Max OAuth tokens (claude setup-token) are not accepted
# here; they only drive the external `claude` agent.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Gemini (native generateContent) -> provider id: gemini
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GEMINI_API_KEY=AIza...
# GOOGLE_API_KEY is honoured as a fallback for GEMINI_API_KEY.
# GEMINI_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions -> provider id: openai-compat
# llama.cpp, Ollama, vLLM, OpenRouter, Groq, Together, LiteLLM, ...
# The base URL is required: there is no default host.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPENAI_COMPAT_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080/v1
# OPENAI_COMPAT_API_KEY=local
# OpenRouter example:
# OPENAI_COMPAT_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# OPENAI_COMPAT_API_KEY=sk-or-...

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Live evidence runners (opt-in; they skip with exit 3 when unset)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# dev/attractor_smoke_live.lg: model for the live pipeline smoke.
# ATTRACTOR_LIVE_MODEL=openai-compat/qwen3.8-27b
# dev/provider_matrix_live.lg: runs for every provider whose key is set;
# the compat entry is opted in by naming a model.
# ATTRACTOR_COMPAT_MODEL=openai-compat/qwen3.8-27b
# Override the default model per native provider (defaults: gpt-4.1-mini,
# claude-sonnet-4-5, gemini-2.5-flash).
# ATTRACTOR_OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4.1-mini
# ATTRACTOR_ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-5
# ATTRACTOR_GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# The management server port is a CLI flag, not an environment variable:
#   bin/attractor serve --port :7070
